# Draft external S22 qualification runner

`s22-run-declared-pair.cjs` remains a draft and has **not launched a qualification pair**.
The existing `s22-run-declared-pair-syntax-check.json` records a successful
`node --check` (exit 0) at `2026-09-28T08:41:27.8894411Z`, scoped to syntax only.
The checked SHA256, `87697d812770a7c3939bcf6498a548c5a6d391b5091a8905e57977f039c2c5f2`,
still matches the unchanged runner bytes. Syntax acceptance does not establish
runtime correctness or qualification readiness.
It creates no manifest and performs no preparation. Root must review the script,
coordinate a quiet machine, freeze the actual hardware/candidate/inputs, and
authorize launch separately. This file is outside the repository by request.

Add the final runner path to the qualification config's `provenance_paths` before
freeze. The script requires its own bytes to be among the immutable manifest
records. A later runner edit therefore requires a new pair. Root supplies the
already frozen manifest, exact declared binary paths, PowerShell 7 executable,
and bundled `NODE_PATH` directory containing Playwright. Run it using the intended
Node executable. It records the Node and PowerShell executable hashes and never
changes the manifest or its registered output roots.

Invocation template (placeholders are not evidence):

```powershell
& $NodeExe 'C:/absolute/evidence/s22-run-declared-pair.cjs' `
  --manifest 'C:/absolute/evidence/pair-manifest.json' `
  --candidate FULL_40_CHARACTER_CANDIDATE_REVISION `
  --native 'C:/absolute/immutable/native-test.exe' `
  --server 'C:/absolute/immutable/spheres-web.exe' `
  --powershell 'C:/Program Files/PowerShell/7/pwsh.exe' `
  --node-path 'C:/absolute/bundled/node_modules' `
  --journal-directory 'C:/absolute/evidence/new-pair-runner-logs'
```

The journal directory's parent must already exist. The directory itself and all
18 declared cell roots must be absent. The runner logs must be disjoint from the
cell roots; in particular browser parents must contain only their one generated
`browser-*` directory. Existing outputs, journals, wrong identities, interleaved
rounds and changed files are rejected. No resume, retry, replacement, pooled
summary, alternate candidate, threshold adjustment or promoted preflight exists.

Cells launch serially in exact manifest order, all nine initial cells before
confirmation. Native arguments enforce `measure`, ordinary budget renewal and
certified capabilities. Browser children get qualification mode, msedge, the
exact expected revision/input SHA/binary/output parent and explicit bundled
`NODE_PATH`; renderer mode is set only for renderer cells. Stale `SPHERES_*` and
`NODE_OPTIONS` values are removed from child environments. All child launches use
`shell: false` and `windowsHide: true`; no visible helper windows are requested.

`journal.jsonl` is create-only and append-only, with flushed start/exit/result
events per cell. Stdout/stderr files are create-only and outside cell outputs.
Known native numerical-limit failures and the harness's explicit browser final
performance failures remain failed measurements and do not select replacements;
the rest of the declared pair continues. Missing/malformed evidence, an unknown
error, an interrupted child, wrong identity or incomplete structural native test
halts the pair and retains all files. A viewer FPS failure occurs before some
later outer-browser observations; it is retained as a failed measurement, never
treated as complete qualification. A failed cell can never be promoted by this
script's result classification; the unchanged verifier makes the final verdict.
Failed native numerical results still require finite consecutive daily rows,
certified facts, exact raw summaries, batch equivalence and intact memory CSV
observations before continuation. A failed final map result requires complete
memory/cold-load/layout evidence and valid workload/raw draw observations; the
final assertion's inclusion of missing accounting does not turn a structural
failure into an ordinary FPS failure. Functional interruptions halt for review.

The runner performs identity hashing and evidence inspection only between cells,
not concurrently with measurements. It neither kills other applications nor
times out a measurement. SIGINT/SIGTERM requests stop the next launch and lets the
owned active child finish naturally. Force-closing the runner can leave a start
without an exit record; that attempt must be retained and investigated, not
resumed into these paths. Browser-driver cleanup remains the existing driver's
responsibility and applies only to its own disposable processes.

Exit 0 means the immutable helper passed both complete rounds; exit 1 means the
pair completed with a failed verdict; exit 2 means a structural/interruption
halt. `verdict.json` is written only after all 18 launches complete. The run summary
is orchestration metadata, not an independent S22 acceptance decision.
